{#
    Who is signed in: a face, a name and an address, the whole of which is the
    way to your own profile — and beside it, the way out.

    The card is a navigation item like any rail row. `NavigationService` claims
    `/profile` for it, so on your profile it is what is lit, and it carries
    `aria-current` like any other.

    Sign-out is a form, because signing out changes state and so takes a POST
    with its CSRF token; it sits here so that it is one click from anywhere,
    as it was in the top bar before.

    `account`  the NavLink for the profile
    `user`     the signed-in User
#}
{% import 'partials/avatar.twig' as avatar %}
<div class="user-card">
    <a class="user-card-link{{ account.active ? ' is-active' : '' }}" href="{{ account.href }}"
       {{ account.active ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>
        {{ avatar.face(user.id, user.displayName, user.initials(), user.avatarPath is not null, 36) }}
        <span class="user-card-text">
            <span class="user-card-name">{{ user.displayName }}</span>
            {# A member added without an address of their own has a placeholder one; it is nobody's to show. #}
            {% if user.canReceiveMail() %}
                <span class="user-card-email">{{ user.email }}</span>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ t('shell.your_profile') }}</span>
        </span>
    </a>
    <form method="post" action="/logout" class="user-card-signout">
        {{ csrf_field() }}
        <button type="submit" class="icon-button" title="{{ t('nav.sign_out') }}">
            {{ icon('sign-out', 'icon-button-icon') }}
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ t('nav.sign_out') }}</span>
        </button>
    </form>
</div>
